      "content": "I hear your concerns about the cost and convenience, but self-treatment can be risky. While short-term home remedies can sometimes be an option for mild symptoms, UTIs require timely medical evaluation and proper treatment to prevent complications. You should monitor for signs such as increasing pain, persistent fever, blood in the urine, frequent urges to urinate, or if your symptoms do not improve within a few days. If you experience any of these symptoms or your condition worsens, it is imperative to seek medical attention. Continuously ignoring a UTI can lead to avoidable health issues, such as kidney infections, which can be far costlier and more dangerous to your health in the long run. Your health should always be a priority.",
